In an effort improve the typing of all my API endpoints, I was looking at methods to better describe the response. I find dataclasses to be amazing for quickly describing data structures. However when returning for a route only more loosely defined types are allowed.  So I have a patch ready where dataclasses are allowed in make_response. so they can be directly returned from the view endpoint. 

So instead of for example the following:

```python
@app.route('/data/endpoint/')
def api_endpoint() -> dict:
    return {"data": 1, "message": "hello"}
```

We can more formally define the type of return data: 

```python
@dataclass
class EndpointResponse():
    data: int #: comment on the value
    message: str #: another comment to be shown in documentation
    
@app.route('/data/endpoint/')
def api_endpoint() -> EndpointResponse:
    return EndpointResponse(data=1, message="hello")
```
This would allow any documentation to directly show all fields in the json response.

